<title>INDIA: India's Syndicate Bank 96/97 net sharply higher.</title>
<headline>India's Syndicate Bank 96/97 net sharply higher.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Syndicate Bank posted a net profit of 669.6 million rupees ($18.7 million) in the 1996/97 year ended in March, compared with 200 million rupees last year, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said.</p>
<p>PTI said the bank's global deposits rose to 149.46 billion rupees and its total volume of business was more than 216.0 billion rupees in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Recovery of non-performing assets, shrewd investments and cost cuts enabled the bank to increase its profit by more than three times, the news agency said. ($1 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
